# Task-breakdown manifest contract — {{ id }}

This file is generated per-run and is AUTHORITATIVE for the epic route's stage 7
(task-breakdown). Copy ids, paths, and shapes from here LITERALLY, substituting only `<tid>`.

## Paths for this run
- Run dir:        `{{ instance_dir }}`
- Outputs dir:    `{{ instance_dir }}/outputs`
- Write tasks.md: `{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks.md`
- Write manifest: `{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks-manifest.json`  (strict JSON, shape below)

## Task ids
Pick one short kebab-case id per epic task: `t<NN>-<slug>` (e.g. `t01-scenario-parser`).
**At most 20 epic tasks.** The emitting task's id is `task-breakdown` — that exact
string is the only `depends_on` value allowed to reference outside this manifest.

## GRANULARITY (avoid auto-compaction)
Slice small. Each `impl` task must be a single cohesive unit (one module/layer/endpoint),
sized so an isolated agent finishes well under its context limit WITHOUT losing the
end goal. Prefer more, smaller tasks over few large ones; express ordering with
`depends_on`, not by bundling. A task that would plausibly need mid-run auto-compaction
is too big — split it.

## Manifest shape

```json
{"tasks": [ ...five entries per epic task... , ...one aggregator... ]}
```

### Per epic task `<tid>` — emit EXACTLY these 5 entries

```json
{"id": "impl1-<tid>", "agent": "developer",
  "instruction": "workflows/routed-runner/instructions/08-implement-task.md",
  "depends_on": ["task-breakdown"],
  "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/design.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks.md"],
  "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/dev-pass-1.md"],
  "timeout_seconds": 10800, "skip_if_outputs_exist": true}

{"id": "test1-<tid>", "agent": "tester",
  "instruction": "workflows/routed-runner/instructions/09-write-tests.md",
  "depends_on": ["impl1-<tid>"],
  "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/design.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/dev-pass-1.md"],
  "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/test-pass-1.md"],
  "timeout_seconds": 10800, "skip_if_outputs_exist": true}

{"id": "review-<tid>", "agent": "reviewer",
  "instruction": "workflows/routed-runner/instructions/10-review-task.md",
  "depends_on": ["test1-<tid>"],
  "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/design.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks.md",
             "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/dev-pass-1.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/test-pass-1.md"],
  "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/review.md"],
  "timeout_seconds": 4800, "skip_if_outputs_exist": true}

{"id": "impl2-<tid>", "agent": "developer",
  "instruction": "workflows/routed-runner/instructions/11-fix-task.md",
  "depends_on": ["review-<tid>"],
  "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/review.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/dev-pass-1.md"],
  "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/dev-pass-2.md"],
  "timeout_seconds": 10800, "skip_if_outputs_exist": true}

{"id": "test2-<tid>", "agent": "tester",
  "instruction": "workflows/routed-runner/instructions/09-write-tests.md",
  "depends_on": ["impl2-<tid>"],
  "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/design.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/dev-pass-2.md"],
  "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid>/test-pass-2.md"],
  "timeout_seconds": 10800, "skip_if_outputs_exist": true}
```

### Aggregator — emit EXACTLY ONE, even when there are ZERO epic tasks

```json
{"id": "aggregate-epic-tasks", "agent": "manager",
  "instruction": "workflows/routed-runner/instructions/12-aggregate.md",
  "depends_on": ["test2-<tid-1>", "test2-<tid-2>", "...one entry per epic task..."],
  "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/tasks/<tid-1>/test-pass-2.md", "...one entry per epic task..."],
  "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/all-tasks-complete.md"],
  "timeout_seconds": 3600, "skip_if_outputs_exist": false}
```

Zero-task edge case: `"depends_on": ["task-breakdown"]`, `"inputs": []` — id and
output path unchanged. The downstream `full-test` task statically waits on
`{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/all-tasks-complete.md`; if the aggregator (or its exact output path) is
missing or renamed, the whole run fails.

### Cross-task dependencies
If task B needs task A's code: add `"test2-<tidA>"` to `impl1-<tidB>`'s `depends_on`
(keeping `"task-breakdown"` there too). Nothing else changes.

## Hard rules (a violation crashes or hangs the run)
1. Strict JSON — no comments, no trailing commas.
2. Every `depends_on` value must be an id in THIS manifest, or the literal string
   `task-breakdown`. Dangling ids crash the engine ungracefully.
3. Ids exactly per the patterns above; globally unique; never reuse a `<tid>`.
4. Aggregator id (`aggregate-epic-tasks`) and its output path: copy EXACTLY.
5. Do not add fields beyond: id, agent, instruction, depends_on, inputs, outputs,
   timeout_seconds, skip_if_outputs_exist.
6. Agent names are exactly: `developer`, `tester`, `reviewer`, `manager`.
